== A.5: the 1-complete class for set coefficients fails two-out-of-three (e -> BC_2 -> e)
functions R -> R: 4 | equivariant: 2
fixed points of R: [] | orbits of R: 1 | points of underlying set: 2

== D.3: composition fails for the weak rational fibrations (E -> B -> [1])
B: objects 2 arrows 5 | composable pairs, triples checked: (11, 23)
E: objects 4 arrows 10 | pairs, triples: (22, 46)
p: E -> B is a covering (unique lifts with prescribed source, and with prescribed target)
fibre of qp over 0: objects 2 arrows 2 components 2
fibre of qp over 1: objects 2 arrows 4 components 1 | exactly one arrow between each ordered pair: True
H^0 with constant rational coefficients: Q^2 over 0 and Q over 1: the direct image of the constant
coefficient along qp is not locally constant, while q (transport e -> BC_2, rationally a constant-
coefficient equivalence) and p (a covering) each have the weak property.
D.12 uses the same two categories: G_disc -> EG is the pullback of e -> BC_2 along EG -> BC_2;
components 2 and 1, so the pullback of a W_0-map along a covering is not in W_0.

== D.4 / D.5: the twisted C_2-extension H of the face poset K of the tetrahedron boundary
K: objects 14 arrows 50 | strict inclusions 36 | chains x<y<z 24
H (cocycle on sigma): objects 14 arrows 100 | composable pairs 440 triples 1552 | components 1 | dim H_1(F_2) = 0
H (cocycle zero): objects 14 arrows 100 | composable pairs 440 triples 1552 | components 1 | dim H_1(F_2) = 1
E (cocycle on sigma): objects 15 arrows 116 | pairs 548 triples 2064 | components 1 | dim H_1(F_2) = 0 | fibre over 0: 1 object, 2 arrows
E (cocycle zero): objects 15 arrows 116 | pairs 548 triples 2064 | components 1 | dim H_1(F_2) = 1 | fibre over 0: 1 object, 2 arrows
Reading: H -> K is a fibration and opfibration with fibre BC_2 and identity transports, so BH -> BK = S^2 is
a homotopy fibre sequence (Quillen's Theorem B) and pi_1(BH) is a quotient of C_2; it is then abelian and
equals H_1. With the cocycle on sigma H_1(F_2) = 0, so BH is simply connected; with the zero cocycle it is C_2.
E retracts onto H up to natural transformation; its fibre over 0 in [1] is BC_2, and BC_2 -> E is not in W_1.
